commit 4ca4f23f8df3f32b9fb573f65e44b5e89c9692c1
Author:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Nov 3 05:40:44 2026 +0700
Commit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Nov 3 05:40:44 2026 +0700

    fix(yang.clojure): D2 token-packet lane — the packet operand is a node; one sibling frame under the machine-data bound
    
    The stashed D2 lowering compiled but every kernel fixture died in the oracle's admission scanner with 'Unexpected AST in context admission'. Instrumenting the rejection with the node itself showed the scanner was right: the entry's plain-vector lane applied the body to the bare symbol dsg__invocation — {:type :application, :operator {:type :variable, :name dsg__body}, :operands [dsg__invocation], :tail? true} — a shape no walker executes ('Unknown AST node type' for any operand whose :type is nil). One token fixes it: (u/v invocation). The scanner's six cases needed no extension (the D2 lowering emits no new node shape once the operand is a node), so its change is diagnostic only: the rejection carries the print-bounded node, and the speculative :let case is dropped (no :let node type exists; u/let1 is an application of a lambda).
    
    The ruling's walker cost is measured, not assumed: 140,142 steps for the budget fixture's 1000 intra-unit calls (140/call) against the two-argument lane's 101,988 (102/call) — the packet build and the token check are dispatch the old direct? flag never executed. The packet is now one variadic conj ([] token args), and the 120k per-call guard, calibrated to the old lane, is recalibrated to 160k with the measurement recorded in the assertion message. The semantic lane measures 75,881. A cheaper dispatch was tried and refused: reading element 0 through dsg__get silently miscompiles programs that define their own get, because that regime's dsg__get reads vectors as nil — the data/vector? guard stays (data/nth refuses non-vectors).
    
    dsg__admitted? and dsg__intra_call share one binding frame again: the stash had split them into nested let1s, and the extra retained helper environment pushed slice8-context-reconstruction's machine-data walk to 100,001 visits against the 100,000 bound. One frame back under, semantics unchanged (both values are pure closure literals; evaluation order is immaterial).
    
    Verified: test-kernel-differential-gate counts {pass 102, recorded-upstream-failure 2, recorded-deviation 2} with blocked 0 and only the by-design unexercised-arity assertion failing; the yang.base JVM lane 124 tests / 1144 assertions / 0 failures 0 errors; the full yang.latte-oracle-test namespace 26 tests / 1895 assertions / 0 errors; clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings on the three touched files. The acceptance budget stays 2,000,000 and the machine-data bound stays 100,000. cljs/cljd lanes not run (JVM verification per the dispatch); the seat schedules them pre-landing as usual.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

