{"role":"assistant","content":"## Verdict: **REJECT — authenticity bypass remains**\n\n### P1: failed token authentication executes the private body\n\nAt `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1097-1102`, vector dispatch is:\n\n```clojure\n(if (= (nth invocation 0) dsg__call_token)\n  (body (nth invocation 1))\n  (body invocation))\n```\n\nThe alternate branch is the defect. A forged vector does not “select nothing”; it is passed directly to the private body as its positional argument vector. Thus `[42]` executes the body with `[42]`, bypassing both the ordinary invocation-record path and token authentication. `[nil [42]]` likewise reaches the body rather than being refused.\n\nThis is precisely the guest-reachable private lane D2 was required to prevent. The token-check alternate must produce an explicit error outcome and **must never apply `body`**.\n\nNo forged-vector regression exists in `test/yang/clojure_test.clj`; the reported verification therefore did not exercise the decisive branch. Add direct-entry tests on both evaluators for at least:\n\n- `[42]`;\n- `[nil [42]]`;\n- an empty vector and an overlong vector;\n- a valid internal packet, proving the authenticated path still works.\n\nThe first three must refuse without entering the body. A side-effecting body can make that non-entry assertion explicit.\n\n### Scanner: acceptable\n\n`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:198-233` remains structural and fail-closed:\n\n- variables must be lexically bound or explicitly admitted globals;\n- only the six real UAST node types are traversed;\n- unknown shapes still throw;\n- the D2 change only adds print-bounded node diagnostics.\n\nNo node-bag admission or speculative `:let` case was introduced. The commit message accurately states that D2 needed no new scanner case after the malformed bare-symbol operand was corrected.\n\n### Exact fixture counts: not supplied or derivable\n\nThe checked-in evidence records the 2M configured budget, outcomes, and executed calls, but no `:steps`. `kernel-c` constructs only `:status`, `:outcome`, `:shape`, and `:executed-calls` (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1820-1833`).\n\nCurrently available measurements are only the microbenchmark’s:\n\n- walker: **140,142** steps;\n- semantic: **75,881** steps.\n\nThe ruling required exact walker and semantic counts for both formerly blocked fixtures. Those remain outstanding and need a counted diagnostic run or harness reporting.\n\n### Additional unrelated regressions to resolve\n\nThe D2 delta also:\n\n- removes the `data/callable?` guard on `dsg__witness` at `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2173-2178`;\n- removes the native-`assoc` implementation of `dsg__assoc`, restoring the slower conj-only path for all dynamic calls.\n\nNeither is required by the token-packet mechanism. Restore the reference behavior or separately justify and test these changes.\n\n**Landing is blocked** on the forged-vector bypass, its adversarial tests, and the exact per-fixture instruction counts. The JVM-only scope with cljs/cljd scheduled before landing is otherwise acceptable, as are the unchanged 2M and 100,000 bounds."}
